165 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 71 0 R
/T (The clipping in the mix compromises the audio quality from the start and turns the mastering engineer's work into a repair job instead of an optimization one. To avoid clipping, it is crucial that the level of the highest peaks of your mix does not exceed -3 dBFS. It is vital that you do not use a limiter on your main bus to increase the volume, as this creates a master with no headroom for us to work with.)
/E (The clipping in the mix compromises the audio quality from the start and turns the mastering engineer's work into a repair job instead of an optimization one. To avoid clipping, it is crucial that the level of the highest peaks of your mix does not exceed -3 dBFS. It is vital that you do not use a limiter on your main bus to increase the volume, as this creates a master with no headroom for us to work with.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
